 "text": "BESbswy BESbswy\nHome\nBartholomew County\nIndiana\nHome\nDepartments\nMeeting Center\nG.I.S.\nCalendar\nHow Do I...\nContact Us\nJob Openings\nADA/TITLE VI\nSearch\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\nBoards, Commissions, & Committees\n|\nCourt Case Lookup\n|\nElected Officials Roster\n|\nFinancials\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\nOrdinances\n|\nView/Pay Taxes Online\n|\nPermitting & Codes\n|\nRoads & Bridges\n|\n|\n|\n|\n|\nSearch the Archives\n|\nSheriff's News\n|\nVeteran News\n|\nVital Records\n|\nFounded in 1821, Bartholomew County is located in the southeastern part of the state with Columbus serving as the county seat. Covering 409 square miles, it lies mostly in the level areas surrounding the East Fork of the White River and its tributaries. The county is intersected by Interstate Highway 65 and U.S. Highway 31 which provide transportation for its commerce, along with one rail line that moves millions of tons of freight through the county annually. Agriculture, manufacturing, and tourism make up the majority of the county's economy.\n19 Oct\n19 Oct 2026\n10:00AM -\nBartholomew County Commissioners' Meeting\n26 Oct\n26 Oct 2026\n10:00AM -\nBartholomew County Commissioners' Meeting\nView Full Calendar\nPhone Listing\nDirections\nCounty News\nEmergency Alerts\nTwitter\nFacebook\nCommunity Links • Terms of Use • Credits & Acknowledgements • Employee Log-In/Out •\n|\n|\nCopyright © Bartholomew County Gov. All Rights Reserved",
